.SH NAME
displayfont \- display linux console font
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBdisplayfont\fR [\fB\-8\fR|\fB\-14\fR|\fB\-16\fR] [\fB\-k\fR[\fBeep\fR]] [\fBfont\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The \fBdisplayfont\fR program displays given \fBfont\fR on console; if \fBfont\fR is
omitted, displays current font. All characters are shown, regardless of their
possible special meaning. The program hardly attempts to restore original
console state, font and unicode mapping after usage. 512\-character fonts are
handled as well.
.SH OPTIONS
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
.IP "\fB\-8\fR, \fB\-14\fR, \fB\-16\fR" 4
.IX Item "-8, -14, -16"
Select font size for files in codepage format (\fB.cp\fR).
.IP \fB\-keep\fR 4
.IX Item "-keep"
Do not restore original font and unicode mapping. May be abbreviated to \fB\-k\fR.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBconsole\fR\|(4), \fBsetfont\fR\|(8), \fBshowconsolefont\fR\|(8).
.SH BUGS
.IX Header "BUGS"
Linux-specific; was not tested on non\-i386 systems.
